Q: IntelliJ IDEA Not Working with OpenJDK24 and JavaFX A: <h2>Java version</h2>
<p>Change <code>source</code> &amp; <code>target</code> from 8 to 24</p>
<p>Per <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79705574/intellij-idea-not-working-with-openjdk24-and-javafx/79706546#comment140598724_79705574">the Comment</a>…</p>
<p>Change this:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>                &lt;configuration&gt;
                    &lt;source&gt;8&lt;/source&gt;
                    &lt;target&gt;8&lt;/target&gt;
                &lt;/configuration&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>… to this:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>                &lt;configuration&gt;
                    &lt;source&gt;24&lt;/source&gt;
                    &lt;target&gt;24&lt;/target&gt;
                &lt;/configuration&gt;
</code></pre>
<h2>OpenJFX version</h2>
<p>And change the version of <code>javafx-controls</code> and <code>javafx-fxml</code> to the same major number as Java. JavaFX/OpenJFX follows the same six-month release train schedule as Java, every March and September.</p>
<p>To determine the latest minor version number, check a Maven repository site like <a href="https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.openjfx/javafx-controls" rel="nofollow noreferrer">this one</a>. For major version 24, that would be <code>24.0.2</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>
        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.openjfx&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;javafx-controls&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;24.0.2&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;
        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.openjfx&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;javafx-fxml&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;24.0.2&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;
        &lt;dependency&gt;
</code></pre>
<h2>Run</h2>
<p>Tell IntelliJ to <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/help/idea/delegate-build-and-run-actions-to-maven.html#maven_reimport" rel="nofollow noreferrer">synchronize the POM</a>. Do a <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/help/idea/work-with-maven-goals.html#run_goal" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Maven <code>clean</code></a>. Run your app.</p>

Q: How do I join with a parameterized view? A: <p>HANA doesn't support passing literal constants to a parameterized view in a JOIN., wrap it in a CTE:</p>
<pre><code>WITH uf AS (
    SELECT &quot;FldValue&quot;, &quot;Trans&quot;, &quot;Descr&quot;
    FROM &quot;q_UFTrans&quot;('OCTG', 'ShowPayment', 9)
)
SELECT T0.&quot;DocEntry&quot;, T0.&quot;GroupNum&quot;, T1.&quot;U_ShowPayment&quot;, T2.&quot;Trans&quot;
FROM &quot;OINV&quot; T0
LEFT JOIN &quot;OCTG&quot; T1 ON T1.&quot;GroupNum&quot; = T0.&quot;GroupNum&quot;
LEFT JOIN uf T2 ON T2.&quot;FldValue&quot; = T1.&quot;U_ShowPayment&quot;
WHERE T0.&quot;DocEntry&quot; = '18057';
</code></pre>

Q: Win32 C++ Generic function to set Cursor from either UI or any worker threads (SetCursor does not work from external threads) A: <p>Yes, you should have <code>SetAppCursor()</code> post/send a message to a window in the UI thread, and then have that window handler call <code>SetCursor()</code> when appropriate.</p>
<p>However, I would suggest a custom message to trigger the change, rather than using <code>WM_SETCURSOR</code> directly. <code>WM_SETCURSOR</code> is a notification message sent by the OS while the mouse is moving over your window. If the mouse is not over your window at the time your worker thread wants to update the cursor, you shouldn't change the cursor immediately and possibly disrupt the user's work. Using a custom message would allow your UI thread to react to the change request without forcing the change to be visible unnecessarily.</p>
<p>For example:</p>
<p>AppCursor.h</p>
<pre><code>void SetAppCursor(bool waiting);
</code></pre>
<p>main.c</p>
<pre><code>...

#define APPWM_SETAPPCURSOR (WM_APP+1)

static UINT uiWaitCount = 0;

void SetAppCursor(bool waiting) {
    PostMessage(hWndMain, APPWM_SETAPPCURSOR, (WPARAM)waiting, 0);
}

static HCURSOR GetWindowClassCursor(HWND hWnd) {
    TCHAR szClassName[256];
    GetClassName(hWnd, szClassName, 256);

    WNDCLASS wc;
    HINSTANCE hInstance = (HINSTANCE)GetWindowLong(hWnd, GWL_HINSTANCE);
    GetClassInfo(hInstance, szClassName, &amp;wc);

    return wc.hCursor;
}

static HCURSOR DetermineCursorForWindow(HWND hWnd) {
    if (uiWaitCount &gt; 0)
        return LoadCursor(NULL, IDC_WAIT);

    HCURSOR hCursor = GetWindowClassCursor(hWnd);
    if (hCursor != NULL)
        return hCursor;

    return LoadCursor(NULL, IDC_ARROW);
}

static void UpdateTheCursorForWindow(HWND hWnd) {
    SetCursor(DetermineCursorForWindow(hWnd));
}

static bool IsMouseInWindow(HWND hWnd) {
    POINT pt;
    GetCursorPos(&amp;pt);
    HWND hWndAtPt = WindowFromPoint(pt);
    while (hWndAtPt) {
        if (hWndAtPt == hWnd) return true;
        hWndAtPt = GetParent(hWndAtPt);
    }
    return false;
}

...

LRESULT WINAPI MainWndProc(HWND hWnd, UINT uMsg, WPARAM wParam, LPARAM lParam) {
    switch (uMsg) {
        case APPWM_SETAPPCURSOR:
            if (wParam != 0)
                ++uiWaitCount;
            else
                --uiWaitCount;
            if (IsMouseInWindow(hWnd))
                UpdateTheCursorForWindow(hWnd);
            return 0;

        case WM_SETCURSOR:
            if (LOWORD(lParam) == HTCLIENT) {
                UpdateTheCursorForWindow(hWnd);
                return TRUE;
            }
            break;
        ...
    }
    return DefWindowProc(hWnd, uMsg, wParam, lParam);
}
</code></pre>
<p>SomeOtherWorkFile.c</p>
<pre><code>#include &quot;AppCursor.h&quot;

// Start Waiting Cursor
SetAppCursor(true);

// ... App Logic ...

// Resume Normal Cursor when done
SetAppCursor(false);
</code></pre>
<p>If you don't want to modify an existing window handler, then you can create a dedicated <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/winmsg/window-features#message-only-windows" rel="nofollow noreferrer">message-only window</a> in the UI thread for <code>SetAppCursor()</code> to post/send its messages to.</p>
